## Styling Architecture

**File**: `src/components/builder/FeaturedStory.scss`

The stylesheet imports design tokens via `@use '../../styles/tokens' as *;` and relies exclusively on CSS custom properties for all theme-sensitive values.

### Theme Awareness

The following tokens adapt automatically when the user switches between light (`white`) and dark (`g100`) themes:

| Token | Light value | Dark value | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `var(--background-primary)` | `#ffffff` | `#161616` | Card background |
| `var(--text-primary)` | `#161616` | `#f4f4f4` | Article title |
| `var(--text-secondary)` | `#525252` | `#c6c6c6` | Description, meta items, meta icons |

The badge colors (`#d0e2ff` background, `#0043ce` text) are hardcoded because they represent a fixed Carbon blue-10/blue-70 design choice from the Figma spec and do not need to adapt to the InsureCo light/dark theme toggle.

### Responsive Behavior

The component uses two breakpoints aligned with Carbon's grid system:

- **< 672px (mobile)**: banner min-height 200px, banner title font-size 36px
- **≥ 672px (tablet/desktop)**: banner min-height 240px, banner title font-size 48px, article title font-size 28px

The footer uses `flex-wrap: wrap` so the CTA button and meta row stack gracefully on narrow viewports without overflow.

### Box Shadow

The card shadow (`0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.10), 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.10)`) is taken directly from the Figma spec and is intentionally not replaced with a design token shadow level, as it is a custom subtle shadow that does not correspond to any of the standard elevation levels in `src/styles/tokens/elevation.scss`.

