## Preview Page

**Route**: `/featured-story-preview`
**File**: `src/pages/FeaturedStoryPreview.jsx`

The preview page renders three configurations of the component side-by-side for visual QA:

1. **Default** — all props at their default values, matching the Figma design exactly.
2. **Custom banner color** — demonstrates that `bannerColor` can be any color (green `#198038` in this case).
3. **Minimal** — `badge`, `readTime`, and `category` all set to empty string to verify the component gracefully hides those elements without layout breaks.

This page is accessible from the app router and serves as the reference view when configuring the component in Builder Publish for the first time.

---

## Adding New Variants or Props

If the component needs to support new editorial patterns (e.g., a background image instead of a solid color, or an author byline):

1. Add the new prop to `FeaturedStory.jsx` with a sensible default.
2. Add the corresponding input object to the `FeaturedStory` entry in `src/builder-registry.js` so it appears in the Builder editor.
3. Add styles to `FeaturedStory.scss` using design tokens — never hardcode colors.
4. Add a new example section to `FeaturedStoryPreview.jsx` that demonstrates the variant.
5. Update this documentation file.

